  "body": "Refs #655\nClaim: cloud/orch\nAuthor model: Opus 5.5 (cloud/orch)\nReviewer model: Fable 5.2 (adversarial-reviewer acdde101)\n\n**Problem.** The #655 inventory (cloud/i655-opus) found four GAP rows that do not match the legacy reference `87fe0d1c`. Its `gap-edit` blocks sit in an issue comment, not in a PR body, so the steward applies them by hand (AGENTS.md §8, ledger-notes).\n\n**Change.** `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md` only, 4 rows: GAP-060 (« Page suivante » button), GAP-080 (reload after a post), GAP-102 (« Bouton + »), GAP-1207 (refresh from the bottom). Generated with `ledger.py fold --from-json` from those blocks, then corrected after Fable round 1 (5 findings, fixed). The GAP-080 ledger-note (its Gap / Source / H.1 cells) is left as is until the operator decides.\n\n**Checks.** Fable 5.2 round 2 APPROVE on a76209ec. `git diff --check` is clean; `check_legacy_pointers.py` reports 0 wrong; the 48 ledger tests pass.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
