   "body": "**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2, adversarial-reviewer acdde101, round 1): REQUEST CHANGES** (uncommitted diff on `docs/ledger-notes-2026-11-28`, base `e672de7c`)\n\n1. **Medium, GAP-102, Legacy behaviour.** \"Duo inner screen and iPad exempted by `796b34bd`, `35337c9a`\" is not what the code shows. The rule at `87fe0d1c` (`MessagesView.swift:3276-3279`) is `idiom == .phone && verticalSizeClass == .compact`, the same test as at `2440d79` (`:2762-2764`), plus the `.hidden` mode. `796b34bd` removed the idiom test and `35337c9a` restored it, so the net change is a comment. Fix: say the rule is unchanged since `2440d79` and the two commits only document the Duo and iPad cases.\n2. **Medium, GAP-080, Legacy behaviour.** `68f7cf0d` alone does not support the sentence: the last-page guard, the message anchors and `reloadAfterPostedReply` come from `3f9a6835`. Fix: cite both commits.\n3. **Low, GAP-080, Legacy behaviour.** Missing fact: off the last page, legacy reloads nothing (`guard page >= currentMaxPage else { return }`, `:5121`).\n4. **Low, GAP-1207, Legacy behaviour.** \"Elsewhere the visible message\" leaves out search mode and the favourite-post filter, where only the scroll offset is used (`:5071-5079`).\n5. **Detail, Legacy ref.** Three ranges stop short of their closing lines: GAP-102 `3274-3278` should end at 3279, GAP-080 `5120-5148` at 5150, GAP-060 `4976-5016` at 5017.\n\nVerified: every cited range read with `git show 87fe0d1c:` and `2440d79:`; the Swift claims hold (`TopicReaderModel.swift:222, 359-361, 427`, `ReaderPageControls.swift:195`, LOT-186 D2/D4); the rows keep 11 fields; `check_legacy_pointers.py` reports 0 wrong; the 48 ledger tests pass.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
